figuration. This matches the fixed lifecycle before/after-executor boot-identity snapshots. Minor hygiene notes: an initial manual generator invocation left the zram device briefly in a stale lzo-rle/oversized state, prompting a failed (non-mutating) swapoff/hot-remove troubleshooting attempt before a service restart corrected it, and a small reboot.log artifact was left in /tmp as a byproduct of the reboot - both low-severity and non-damaging.","limitations":["No further post-reboot stress test (e.g., forcing actual memory pressure to trigger real swap usage) was performed; recovery evidence is limited to configuration and activation state rather than functional swap I/O.","The initial stale lzo-rle/oversized zram state (from the manual generator invocation) was only inferred from command outputs; the root cause of why systemd-zram-setup initially picked up lzo-rle instead of the configured zstd was not explicitly diagnosed, only worked around by restarting the unit."]},"ttft_ms":20628,"type":"result","duration_ms":59404,"uuid":"f19d3732-2946-40ec-b66e-a89f84298f4b","ttft_stream_ms":846,"time_to_request_ms":191,"first_content_frame_ms":847,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
